For every compactly supported real law, $$\label{eq:entropy-smoothing}
 \mathcal H_s(X)=h(X+V_s)-\log s,
 \qquad
 \mathcal H_s(aX+b)=\mathcal H_{s/|a|}(X)
 \quad(a\ne0).$$ If $t/s=N$ is a positive integer, then $G_{s,t}$ is concave in the law, $$\label{eq:entropy-integer-window}
 0\le G_{s,t}\le\log N,
 \qquad G_{s,t}(X+Y)\ge G_{s,t}(X)$$ for independent bounded $X,Y$. For arbitrary $z\ge s>0$, $$\label{eq:entropy-scale-comparison}
 \mathcal H_s-\log(z/s+2)\le\mathcal H_z\le\mathcal H_s+1.$$ Furthermore, $$\label{eq:entropy-grid-comparison}
 |\mathcal H_s(X)-H_s^0(X)|\le1,
 \qquad |H_s^0(X+b)-H_s^0(X)|\le1.$$

Let $\nu$ be a compactly supported exact-dimensional probability measure on $\mathbb R$ of dimension $d$. Then $$\label{eq:entropy-dimension-upper}
 \limsup_{s\downarrow0}
 \frac{\max\{\mathcal H_s(\nu),H_s^0(\nu)\}}
 {\log(1/s)}\le d.$$

Let $X$ be bounded and $J$ an independent fair bit. For $0<s<v<t$, $$\label{eq:two-point-gain}
 G_{s,t}(X+vJ)-G_{s,t}(X)
 \ge\Delta_v(X)-s/v-v/t.$$ The same estimate holds for convolution with any fair two-point law whose two points have distance $v$.

For a system satisfying <a href="#eq:types-loss" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="eq:types-loss">[eq:types-loss]</a>, with the parameters <a href="#eq:types-parameters" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="eq:types-parameters">[eq:types-parameters]</a> and conditional laws <a href="#eq:types-laws" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="eq:types-laws">[eq:types-laws]</a>, for every $n\ge1$ and $s>0$ we have $$\begin{aligned}
 \mathbb EH(\nu_{\omega,n})
 &=H(G_{bn}\mid\Omega_n)
 \ge nh_b,\label{eq:types-exact-entropy}\\
 \mathbb EH_s^0(\nu_{\omega,n})
 &\le H_s^0(\mu)+1.\label{eq:types-grid-entropy}
\end{aligned}$$ Moreover, there are $\varepsilon>0$ and an integer $n_0$ such that for every $n\ge n_0$, $$\label{eq:types-deficit}
 \mathbb E\!\left[\mathbf1_{E_n}
    \bigl(H(\nu_{\omega,n})-H_{\rho_n}^0(\nu_{\omega,n})\bigr)
    \right]\ge\varepsilon n.$$

Under the assumptions and notation of Lemma <a href="#lem:type-deficit" data-reference-type="ref" data-reference="lem:type-deficit">8</a>, there exist $c>0$ and an integer $n_0$ such that, for each $n\ge n_0$, there is a deterministic finite integer $B_n\ge a_n$ satisfying $$\label{eq:types-pair-bands}
 \mathbb E\!\left[\mathbf1_{E_n}
       \sum_{\ell=a_n}^{B_n}c_\ell(
u_{\omega,n})ight]\ge cn.$$ Here $c_\ell(
u)$ is the maximum total weight of fair two-point laws with separations in $[2^{-\ell},2^{1-\ell})$ whose weighted sum is a submeasure of $
u$, as in Lemma <a href="#lem:pair-bound" data-reference-type="ref" data-reference="lem:pair-bound">7</a>. The constants $b,A,A',c,n_0$ are independent of $n$ and $\omega$; no growth bound on $B_n$ is asserted.

For all integers $j\ge0$, $n\ge1$, and $L\ge1$, with $g_j$ as in <a href="#eq:window-entropy" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="eq:window-entropy">[eq:window-entropy]</a>, $$\label{eq:conditional-gain}
 \mathbb E\bigl[g_j-g_{j+n}\mid\mathcal F_{j+n}\bigr]
 \ge \frac{\delta}{2}
 c_{L-\lceil\sigma_j\rceil}(\nu_{\theta^j\omega,n}).$$

For each fixed environment and target $L\in\{1,\ldots,T\}$, all the retained windows in <a href="#eq:retention" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="eq:retention">[eq:retention]</a> are pairwise disjoint. Consequently, $$\label{eq:telescoping-windows}
 \sum_{i=1}^q\sum_{j\in J_i}
 \mathbf1_{\mathcal A_{i,j,L}}(g_j-g_{j+n_i})
 \le2\log M.$$
